<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iona</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iona is a small island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-hebrides">Inner Hebrides</a> off the west coast of Mull in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a> founded a monastery there in 563, which became the head of a network of churches and the centre of the mission to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> and Northumbria; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-kells">Book of Kells</a> was probably begun there. Raided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> from 795, it remained a burial place of Scottish kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iona.jpg" alt="Iona" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lisa Stevens from Sutton Coldfield, UK · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iona_(15020668711).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
